# Modelfile: Qwen3.5-9B (dense), 64K context — "64k-agentic" tuning, sized
# to fit Copilot CLI / opencode's static tool-schema overhead, same
# rationale as qwen3.6__35b-a3b-64k-agentic/Modelfile: Copilot CLI's system
# prompt + all built-in tool schemas (bash, edit, view, grep, glob, task,
# plus the GitHub MCP server) measured at ~21,504 input tokens *before* any
# real conversation (see docs/tuning-results.md). That's 65% of a 32K
# window by itself, so — same as the 35B tiers — this needed to jump
# straight to 64K rather than stopping at 32K.
#
# IMPORTANT — read before defaulting to this over qwen3.6:35b-a3b-*-agentic:
# qwen3.5:9b is DENSE (not MoE). Empirically measured on this host (8GB
# VRAM, `ollama ps`, no num_gpu override):
#
#   num_ctx    GPU split      gen tok/s   prompt-eval tok/s
#   65,536     74%/26% GPU    22.3         98.9
#
# vs. qwen3.6:35b-a3b-64k-agentic (MoE, ~3B active) at the same context:
#   78%/22% GPU split, 36.6 gen tok/s, 247.1 prompt-eval tok/s
#
# The MoE model is *faster* here despite being ~4x the total size — a
# dense model must run 100% of its weights on whatever fraction lands on
# CPU once it stops fitting fully in VRAM, whereas MoE only runs its small
# active-expert subset even on CPU-offloaded layers. So at this context
# size, qwen3.5:9b's usual speed advantage (see 12k-standalone) has
# already mostly evaporated.
#
# Practical guidance: use this tier when you specifically want the much
# smaller footprint (7.6GB vs 22GB — leaves far more RAM/VRAM headroom for
# other apps) or want a second, independently-loadable model alongside
# qwen3.6:35b-a3b-*-agentic (e.g. opencode `/model` switching for quick
# tool-calling questions). For heavy/long agentic sessions where raw
# throughput matters most, prefer qwen3.6:35b-a3b-128k-agentic — it stays
# faster even while spilling to CPU. See docs/tuning-results.md
# ("qwen3.5:9b tuning") for the full writeup.
#
# num_batch left at 256 (not dropped to 128 like the 35B's 96K/128K fix) —
# tested here too: 128 made no measurable difference to this model's
# GPU/CPU split at 64K or 128K, so there's no reason to trade away
# prompt-eval throughput for it.
#
# num_gpu intentionally omitted — see 12k-standalone/Modelfile for why.

FROM qwen3.5:9b

PARAMETER num_ctx 65536
PARAMETER num_batch 256
PARAMETER num_thread 16

# Sampling aligned the same way as qwen3.5__9b-12k-standalone/Modelfile —
# see that file and docs/tuning-results.md ("Unsloth alignment") for the
# full reasoning.
PARAMETER temperature 0.6
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER presence_penalty 0.0

# Matches qwen3.6:35b-a3b-64k-agentic's split exactly (16384/49152) so the
# same COPILOT_PROVIDER_MAX_PROMPT_TOKENS/MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS math applies —
# see configs/copilot/copilot-byok-9b-64k-agentic.env.
PARAMETER num_predict 16384

SYSTEM """You are a helpful assistant. Keep your internal reasoning
efficient and proportional to the difficulty of the question — do not
over-deliberate on simple requests. Regardless of how much you have
reasoned, always make sure to produce a clear, complete final answer
before you finish; if you notice you are running low on room to respond,
wrap up your reasoning early and give your best answer rather than leaving
it incomplete.
"""
